1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,435
The third arc closed with a lunch that was supposed to be a victory.

2
00:00:03,435 --> 00:00:13,657
The transferred project had continued for six weeks without Lin; the participant numbers were abundant, and every volunteer had stayed.

3
00:00:13,657 --> 00:00:18,136
“Nobody expected that,” the spokeswoman said.

4
00:00:18,136 --> 00:00:24,910
Her joy was real, and so was her insistence that the report mention the last setback.

5
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:36,332
Suddenly there was an incentive to do what nobody had asked: part of the money was for the ongoing work, and any of the million small tasks could now be paid.

6
00:00:36,332 --> 00:00:42,200
Each of them had an eye on the door, and no one sat still.

7
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:44,805
He was not triumphant.

8
00:00:44,805 --> 00:00:52,078
Sitting in his overcoat, he watched the rain and felt an ache in his thumb from carrying boxes.

9
00:00:52,078 --> 00:00:55,512
“We invested a year,” he said.

10
00:00:55,512 --> 00:00:58,167
“Some of it was a triumph.

11
00:00:58,167 --> 00:01:05,995
Most of it was not.” A few of the guests agreed; several did not.

12
00:01:05,995 --> 00:01:14,463
A jealous colleague, a drunk broker, and a defiant young man from the hut settlement all spoke at the luncheon.

13
00:01:14,463 --> 00:01:19,606
“Nowadays everybody wants a conqueror,” the broker said.

14
00:01:19,606 --> 00:01:29,064
“You want a blackboard.” The relevance of the remark was not obvious to anyone, least of all to him.

15
00:01:29,064 --> 00:01:34,493
The frustrating part was the handwriting on the report: his own.

16
00:01:34,493 --> 00:01:45,080
Oftentimes the least influential person in the room writes the document that sways the room, and he had written it without noticing which side he was on.

17
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:49,724
“Do not continue out of laziness,” Maya said.

18
00:01:49,724 --> 00:01:59,937
“Continue out of impulse, if you must, but keep the shelter open, and do not raise a fist at the people who read it.”

19
00:01:59,937 --> 00:02:04,691
Several participants disapproved of the final paragraph.

20
00:02:04,691 --> 00:02:16,363
A hat and a glove were, quite simply, not a policy, and the insistent demand for a cleaner number could not be met without deleting somebody's name.

21
00:02:16,363 --> 00:02:20,717
Many of them would persevere; some would not.

22
00:02:20,717 --> 00:02:26,955
“The interviewee is not the interviewee of the question,” the spokeswoman said.

23
00:02:26,955 --> 00:02:37,048
“That is why we keep asking.” The question, at least, had survived the defeat, and there was no shame in that.

24
00:02:37,048 --> 00:02:47,920
“Shit,” the broker said, when the final total appeared on the screen; he was immensely relieved, and he said so, twice.

25
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:55,931
The promise had survived the pressure, and the price of it had a name in every room they entered.
